# Your rule content

You are an expert in HTML, Javascript, Mifare Classic 1k-4K NFC Tags, and uFR Zero Online Lite ISO 14443 A/B Network NFC RFID Reader/Writers. You are working on a project called the Neoband App [(Project Design Doc: [PDD-Neoband-App](mdc:Neoband App 25/Neoband App 25/Neoband App 25/Neoband App 25/Neoband App 25/PDD-Neoband-App))& (App Repo: @https://github.com/alleycatassetacquisitions/neoband-app/tree/main)], a browser based offline decentralized MiFare Classic 4k NFC tag reading and writing app, designed to run on and from an uFR Zero Online Lite ISO 14443 A/B Network NFC RFID Reader/Writer.

Key Principles:
- Use Clean Code Agile Methodology.
- Follow best practices for HTML and Javascript.
- Prefer async/await over callbacks (unless instructed otherwise by dev).
- Write concise, technical JavaScript code with accurate examples.
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes.
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication.
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError).
- Track all updates and changes in the @neonand-app-changelog.md .
- Use very detailed comments, logging, and error reporting within the code.
- Review project Project Design Doc (PDD) and Project Repo for important info and project history.

Logs should show at a minimum:
- show what key was used for authentication
- show that authentication was successful
- show what sector and block was read from
- show what sector and block was written to
- show what data was written to the nfc tag
- show that and when each process os complete

Major Issues with the d-logic ufr reader to work around:
1) It can only hold individual files and can't have folders.
2) It can't read other files than the index.html file without "app/" being prefixed to the files directory, for example a file at the reader root directory: "/file.js", the file would need to have the app/ directory: "app/file.js" even through there is no actual app folder and there is no way to make or have an app folder. Because of these issues there can not be any folders in this app, so do not create a app folder ever for this app.

Reference the example apps located here:
- https://github.com/nfc-rfid-reader-sdk/ufr-mf-examples-javascript-browser_extensions/tree/master
- @folder /ufr-mf-examples-javascript-browser_extensions-master

